# ── Firebase (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create project at https://console.firebase.google.com
# Project Settings → Your apps → Web app → copy config
# (Firebase web config is public by design; security comes from Firestore rules.)
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── AI: pick ONE mode ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# A) Server proxy (use this for any deployed site). The key stays on the server.
#    Set these in Vercel → Project → Environment Variables (NOT prefixed with VITE_):
#      OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
#      FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=<same as VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID>
#      AI_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini            (optional)
#    and enable it in the client:
# VITE_AI_PROXY=true

# B) Local development only. ⚠ Anything prefixed VITE_ is bundled into the
#    public JavaScript: never set these on a deployed site, anyone can read them.
# VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# C) Nothing here: each user pastes their own key in Settings (stored in their browser).
